[ti:Amor Fati]
[ar:EdgarAllanMusic]
[al:EcceH.text (Revalued)]
[00:32.67]Autumn noon, the grapes are browning
[00:37.28]Not a ripple on the lake
[00:41.50]I looked behind me, then ahead
[00:45.04]And nothing asked to be remade
[00:51.00]Forty-four, I laid the year down
[00:55.37]It had the right to go
[00:59.46]Whatever in it was alive
[01:02.27]Is saved, and won't grow old
[01:08.17]Let it all come round again
[01:13.03]The fever and the wine
[01:17.10]I wouldn't change a single hour
[01:21.63]Amor fati, it was mine
[01:42.40]By the lake at Silvaplana
[01:45.12]A pyramid of stone
[01:46.73]Six thousand feet past man and time
[01:49.54]The thought struck me alone
[01:51.64]Not a sigh disturbs the open sea
[01:54.11]I'd never wish it new
[01:56.06]The future spreads like broad, calm water
[01:58.88]I wouldn't change its blue
[02:00.76]Let it all come round again
[02:05.59]The sickness and the shore
[02:09.67]I wouldn't move a single stone
[02:14.16]Amor fati, nothing more
[02:19.28]Not only bear what has to be
[02:22.94]Love it, all of it, and stay
[02:53.02]Let it all come round again
[02:57.82]The darkness and the bloom
[03:02.18]How could I not be thankful
[03:06.37]To every hour, even the tomb
[03:14.94]Amor fati
[03:19.77]Even the tomb
[03:25.16]
